，但65%（13例）患者发生3级以上irAE，包括3例（15%）心肌炎。irAE发生时间较早（中位 onset 42天）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析 (Post-FMT)\",\n            \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的菌群结构显著分离（p=0.03）。响应者体内多胺和胆汁酸水平升高。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"免疫表型分析\",\n            \"finding\": \"响应者中耗竭性T中央记忆细胞和T效应记忆细胞升高；未响应者中CD28和IL10等免疫耗竭标志物升高。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"irAE与供体/菌群关联 (Melanoma)\",\n            \"finding\": \"13例发生3级以上irAE的患者中，6例（46%）接受了同一供体（D5）的FMT。D5供体的菌群与其他供体显著不同（p<0.01），具有高相对丰度的Prevotella copri。P. copri定植信号与irAE发展相关。接受D5供体FMT的NSCLC患者未出现类似irAE。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"肠道屏障功能\",\n            \"finding\": \"发生3级以上irAE的患者在FMT后sST2（渗漏肠标志物）水平显著升高（p=0.002）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"无菌小鼠模型\",\n            \"finding\": \"仅当响应者（R）基线粪便随后跟随其对应供体粪便灌胃时，才导致α多样性和定植物种数随时间显著增加（p<0.01）；非响应者（NR）基线粪便无论是否跟随供体粪便，均未改变多样性或定植。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已有试验显示FMT联合抗PD-1可改善黑色素瘤对ICIs的反应，但FMT联合抗PD-1在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）中的临床影响，以及FMT联合双ICI（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）在黑色素瘤中的微生物组变化、免疫shift及临床后果尚不清楚。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"两项早期探索性临床试验：1) 20例晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者接受一线抗PD-1单药治疗联合粪菌移植（FMT）；2) 20例晚期黑色素瘤患者接受一线双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4，dual ICI）联合FMT。所有患者均接受来自11名不同健康供体（HD）的口服FMT。研究还包含无菌（GF）小鼠模型以验证定植机制。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"该研究旨在评估FMT在增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效及调节毒性方面的作用，特别是在此前证据不足的NSCLC和双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤中。研究招募了40例患者，分别进行NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（双ICI）治疗，并在肠道准备后给予FMT。主要终点为客观缓解率（ORR）。通过鸟枪法宏基因组学、代谢组学（HPLC）、蛋白质组学（Olink）和流式细胞术对患者样本进行分析，并在小鼠模型中验证菌群定植情况。结果显示，在NSCLC中ORR为80%且无3级以上免疫相关不良事件（irAE），而在黑色素瘤中ORR为75%但65%患者出现3级以上irAE，包括心肌炎。研究发现响应者与未响应者术后菌群聚类分离，响应者体内多胺和胆汁酸增加，而未响应者显示免疫耗竭标志物升高。此外，特定供体（D5）携带的高丰度Prevotella copri与黑色素瘤患者的严重irAE相关。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"背景与安全性考量\",\n            \"material\": \"FMT联合双ICI（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）导致高比例严重irAE（包括心肌炎），且发生时间早于既往报告。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"在综述中讨论FMT临床应用的安全性挑战，特别是当与强效免疫治疗方案联用时，需警惕过度激活免疫系统导致的自身免疫毒性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"生物标志物开发\",\n            \"material\": \"基线菌群、供体特异性菌群（如P. copri）、代谢产物（多胺、胆汁酸）及免疫表型可作为预测响应和毒性的潜在标志物。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"支持综述中关于“精准微生物组医学”的讨论，即如何利用微生物组数据筛选适合FMT的患者或优化供体选择策略。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅限早期探索性研究，无对照组，结果可能受选择偏倚影响。不能直接推断普适性疗效。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在实体瘤中的客观缓解率（ORR）数据：NSCLC中80%，黑色素瘤中75%。同时指出毒性谱系的巨大差异：NSCLC无3级以上irAE，而黑色素瘤双ICI组高达65%。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“肠道微生物组如何调节ICI在实体瘤中的疗效”这一子问题，具体展示FMT作为辅助手段在不同肿瘤类型和ICI方案下的疗效潜力及局限性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制多为相关性发现，需结合其他研究验证因果关系。P. copri与irAE的关联仅在黑色素瘤双ICI组中显著，在NSCLC单药组中未观察到，提示情境依赖性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"揭示了潜在的机制线索：1) 响应者菌群特征（多胺、胆汁酸升高）；2) 毒性机制关联（P. copri定植与irAE，特别是心肌炎，以及肠道渗漏标志物sST2升高）；3) 免疫表型差异（响应者T细胞记忆亚群 vs 未响应者耗竭标志物）。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“哪些机制介导了这种效应”这一子问题，提供微生物-宿主互作的具体分子和细胞层面证据，特别是关于毒性发生的潜在微生物驱动因素。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文提供了FMT联合ICI治疗实体瘤的临床效果对比数据，特别是揭示了不同ICI骨架（单药vs双药）对FMT诱导毒性的调节作用。它识别出特定菌群（P. copri）与严重irAE的关联，以及响应者特有的代谢产物（多胺、胆汁酸）和免疫表型变化。这些内容可用于综述中讨论FMT的临床获益/风险平衡、毒性机制及生物标志物预测。\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"本研究为单臂、非随机、小样本探索性研究，结论仅为假设生成性质，不能作为确证性证据。\",\n          \"NSCLC和黑色素瘤的结果不可互换外推，不同ICI方案（单药vs双药）对毒性有显著调节作用。\",\n          \"P. copri与irAE的关联仅在特定供体和特定治疗背景下观察到，需谨慎解读其普遍意义。\",\n          \"无菌小鼠模型的定植结果不能完全代表复杂人体环境中的菌群动态。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT)\",\n          \"Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICI)\",\n          \"Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)\",\n          \"Melanoma\",\n          \"Immune-related Adverse Events (irAEs)\",\n          \"Gut Microbiome Profiling (Shotgun Metagenomics)\",\n          \"Prevotella copri\",\n          \"Polyamines and Bile Salts\",\n          \"T cell exhaustion markers (CD28, IL10)\",\n          \"Leaky gut markers (sST2)\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"identity\",\n            \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n            \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n            \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n            \"status\": \"partial\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n            \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n            \"status\": \"partial\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\55e5f184350846573ce6b2d40fdcbd15f2602f90\\\\fe6455704805c8dbacd86cc388cca0ba\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n      \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch6.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_634b345179\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"As a narrative review, the authors conducted a literature search and synthesis of both preclinical (animal models) and clinical studies. They organized the discussion around three main themes: the general influence of gut microbiota on ICI efficacy, the relationship between microbiota and irAEs (specifically myocarditis), proposed molecular mechanisms (molecular mimicry, Treg suppression, cytokine networks), and therapeutic applications (antibiotics, other drugs like PPIs/statins). The approach relies on interpreting correlations and mechanistic hypotheses from cited works rather than conducting new primary experiments.\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides a structured synthesis of the 'gut-heart axis' in the context of cardio-oncology, linking specific microbial taxa (Flexispira, Ruminococcaceae, Bacteroides) to ICI-associated myocarditis pathology based on available preclinical and clinical data.\",\n            \"limits\": \"The review is narrative and does not present a systematic meta-analysis. Most mechanistic insights are inferred from animal models or other irAEs; direct clinical evidence for microbiota causality in myocarditis is limited. The therapeutic potential of microbiota modulation remains hypothetical and unvalidated in human trials.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Highlights the critical trade-off between using antibiotics to prevent myocarditis and their potential to compromise ICI anti-tumor efficacy, identifying this as a key research gap.\",\n            \"limits\": \"Does not provide quantitative data on the magnitude of this trade-off across different cancer types or ICI regimens. The heterogeneity of cardiac adverse events across cancer types is noted but not analyzed.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Preclinical mouse models treated with PD-1 inhibitors\",\n            \"finding\": \"Depletion of specific gut bacteria (e.g., Flexispira, Ruminococcaceae) using antibiotics reduced inflammatory cell infiltration and myocardial injury area. Conversely, these bacteria showed positive correlations with cardiac injury markers and negative correlations with cardioprotective factors.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Clinical observations of patients with irAEs\",\n            \"finding\": \"Patients developing severe irAEs, including myocarditis, exhibited higher abundance of pathobionts and decreased relative abundance of Ruminococcaceae. Bacteroides levels dynamically changed during irAE onset and remission.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic hypotheses derived from preclinical and autoimmune data\",\n            \"finding\": \"Proposed mechanisms include molecular mimicry where microbial epitopes cross-react with heart tissue, and dysbiosis leading to suppressed Treg function and amplified pro-inflammatory cytokine responses (e.g., CXCL9/10, TNF-α).\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"To synthesize existing evidence on the link between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis, identify underlying molecular mechanisms, and evaluate the potential of modulating gut microbiota (e.g., via antibiotics, transplantation) as a therapeutic strategy, while addressing the balance between reducing irAEs and maintaining anti-tumor efficacy.\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the association between gut microbiota and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI)-associated myocarditis, a severe immune-related adverse event (irAE). It synthesizes evidence from preclinical studies (primarily mouse models) and clinical observations to explore molecular mechanisms and potential therapeutic interventions involving microbiota modulation.\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review aims to elucidate the role of gut microbiota in the pathogenesis of ICI-associated myocarditis. The authors hypothesize that gut microbiota influences this condition through mechanisms such as molecular mimicry, regulation of regulatory T cells (Tregs), and systemic inflammation. The paper discusses how specific microbial alterations correlate with cardiac injury markers and reviews preclinical evidence suggesting that antibiotic depletion or modulation of gut flora can mitigate myocardial damage. However, it highlights the controversy surrounding antibiotic use due to potential negative impacts on ICI efficacy and notes that clinical validation for microbiota-targeted therapies is still pending.\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Contextual background on the 'gut-heart axis' and the severity of ICI-associated myocarditis.\",\n            \"material\": \"The review establishes myocarditis as a high-mortality (25%-50%) complication of ICIs and introduces the concept of the gut-heart axis in cardiovascular disease, extending it to cardio-oncology.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To provide background on why ICI-associated myocarditis is a critical safety concern and to frame the microbiome's role within a broader physiological system.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Identification of specific microbial biomarkers associated with irAEs.\",\n            \"material\": \"Associations between pathobiont abundance, decreased Ruminococcaceae, and dynamic changes in Bacteroides with irAE onset/remission.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To suggest potential microbial signatures that could serve as predictive biomarkers for severe immune-related adverse events, although clinical utility is not yet proven.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Discussion of confounding medications (PPIs, statins) affecting the microbiome.\",\n            \"material\": \"Long-term PPI use reduces diversity and may increase irAE risk; statins may mitigate inflammation.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To highlight potential confounders in microbiome studies and suggest that concomitant medications may alter the baseline microbiome-immune interaction, necessitating stratified analysis in future research.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"These mechanisms are largely inferred from preclinical studies or other irAEs (colitis, dermatitis) and are explicitly stated as requiring further validation in myocarditis. The causal chain is not yet established in humans.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides detailed mechanistic hypotheses for how gut microbiota might mediate immune-related adverse events, specifically focusing on molecular mimicry (cross-reactivity between microbial epitopes and cardiac tissues) and the suppression of Tregs by dysbiosis. It also outlines cytokine pathways (CXCL9/10, TNF-α) recruited by microbiota-derived signals.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to explain the biological plausibility of microbiome-mediated immune dysregulation beyond just tumor response, offering a parallel mechanism for toxicity. Helps contextualize why certain microbes are linked to organ-specific damage.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"The review does not provide specific data on how microbiota modulation affects tumor response rates in solid tumors; its focus is on the adverse event aspect. The claim about antibiotic compromising efficacy is supported by retrospective studies cited, but the review itself does not generate new efficacy data.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Discusses the dual role of gut microbiota in influencing ICI outcomes: enhancing anti-tumor immunity (via CD8+ T cell expansion) while simultaneously increasing the risk of irAEs. It notes that antibiotic use to mitigate irAEs may compromise ICI efficacy.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Useful for discussing the complex interplay between microbiota, efficacy, and toxicity. It highlights that strategies targeting the microbiome must balance these competing outcomes.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"This review serves as a conceptual bridge connecting gut microbiome composition to ICI-associated myocarditis, a specific irAE. It offers mechanistic hypotheses (molecular mimicry, Treg modulation) and identifies specific microbial signatures associated with cardiac injury. While it does not directly address the modulation of ICI *efficacy* in solid tumors (its focus is on toxicity), it provides crucial context on how microbiota influences immune outcomes broadly, which may be relevant for understanding the side-effect profile of effective treatments.\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"The paper is a narrative review, not a systematic review or empirical study; findings represent synthesized interpretations rather than primary data.\",\n          \"Mechanisms described (e.g., molecular mimicry, Treg suppression) are largely derived from preclinical models or extrapolated from other irAEs; direct causal evidence in human ICI-myocarditis is lacking.\",\n          \"Therapeutic suggestions (antibiotics, transplantation) are presented as future possibilities based on preclinical success; clinical application is explicitly stated as distant and controversial.\",\n          \"The review focuses on toxicity (myocarditis) rather than efficacy; do not infer conclusions about tumor response modulation from this text without caution.\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n          \"Molecular mimicry in ICI-induced autoimmunity\",\n          \"Regulatory T cells (Tregs) and gut microbiota interaction\",\n          \"Antibiotic-mediated microbiota depletion in preclinical models\",\n          \"Bacteroides and Ruminococcaceae dynamics in irAEs\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_634b345179\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0590\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiome in colorectal cancer: recent advances and clinical implications\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.3393/ac.2026.00010.0001\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286044272\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch6.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0590\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-f45b87be8e30256e\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\phase_iii_rct_evidence\\\\attempt-c7j_i2fn\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_a86301e06d\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"采用叙事性综述方法，按主题组织材料：1) 病理机制：分类介绍主要致病菌株的分子通路；2) 保护机制：阐述有益菌群及代谢物的稳态维持功能；3) 诊断应用：汇总近期宏基因组学筛查研究的性能指标（AUC等）及局限性分析；4) 治疗干预：对比不同微生物调控策略（饮食、益生菌、FMT、工程菌、抗生素）的临床前与临床证据。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了结直肠癌相关微生物致病机制的系统性分类框架，明确了病原体与宿主免疫/代谢通路的交互细节。\",\n            \"limits\": \"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究，未提供新的实验数据；对临床转化的建议基于现有证据等级的综合判断，而非独立验证。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"指出了微生物标志物研究中混杂因素（如BMI、粪便特征）的重要性，强调了定量分析和去混杂的必要性。\",\n            \"limits\": \"未提供具体的去混杂统计模型代码或通用阈值，仅引用了相关研究案例。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"区分了不同微生物治疗策略的证据层级，明确将FMT和工程菌定位为实验性干预，纠正了过度乐观的临床预期。\",\n            \"limits\": \"对于特定菌株在人类患者中的长期定植效果和安全性数据，材料指出尚不充分。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"针对具核梭杆菌 (Fn)、pks+大肠杆菌、ETBF等主要病原体\",\n            \"finding\": \"这些菌株通过激活Wnt/β-catenin、NF-κB等信号通路，诱导DNA损伤、慢性炎症及免疫抑制，直接促进肿瘤发生和进展。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"针对基于粪便宏基因组学的CRC筛查模型\",\n            \"finding\": \"多队列荟萃分析显示宏基因组面板具有高诊断效能（AUC 0.85-0.99），但部分关联信号受肠道转运时间、炎症状态等宿主因素混杂，去混杂后某些标志物（如Fn）的关联性减弱。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"针对FMT及其他微生物疗法\",\n            \"finding\": \"FMT在黑色素瘤等实体瘤中改善免疫检查点抑制剂疗效有初步证据，但在CRC中仅限小规模无对照试验，存在安全性和生态稳定性风险；益生菌和工程菌主要处于临床前阶段；抗生素暴露与CRC风险增加相关，不建议作为预防或治疗手段。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"旨在澄清肠道微生物组在结直肠癌中从“旁观者”到“主动驱动者”的角色转变，评估当前基于微生物组的诊断 biomarkers 和治疗手段的临床证据水平、主要障碍及未来转化方向。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"结直肠癌（CRC）与肠道微生物组的关系，涵盖致癌机制、保护性菌群功能、基于微生物组的生物标志物开发及临床治疗策略。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本文是一篇综述，系统梳理了肠道微生物组在结直肠癌发生发展中的主动驱动作用及其临床转化潜力。文章首先详细阐述了多种病原体（如具核梭杆菌、pks+大肠杆菌等）通过炎症、代谢紊乱、基因毒性和免疫逃逸促进肿瘤发生的分子机制，并介绍了有益菌群及其代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸）的保护作用。随后，文章评估了基于粪便宏基因组学的生物标志物研究进展，指出其在早期检测中的高准确性但面临标准化和混杂因素控制的挑战。最后，综述了饮食调节、益生菌、粪菌移植（FMT）及工程菌等治疗策略的证据等级，强调目前多数疗法仍处于实验或早期临床阶段，且抗生素使用可能增加风险。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提供结直肠癌中微生物组与宿主互作的整体背景，区分致癌病原体与保护性菌群。\",\n            \"material\": \"概述了CRC相关病原体的致病途径（炎症、基因毒性、屏障破坏）及有益菌群的稳态维持作用。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为综述的背景部分，界定研究对象（CRC微生物组）的功能谱系，帮助读者理解为何特定微生物会影响癌症进程及治疗响应。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提供关于微生物组检测技术现状和挑战的信息。\",\n            \"material\": \"讨论了宏基因组学筛查的性能、混杂因素（如粪便特征、BMI）的影响及标准化的必要性。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"用于讨论在评估微生物组与免疫治疗关系时，需要控制的技术变量和混杂因素，强调定量分析和去混杂的重要性。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"主要证据来自结直肠癌的体外/体内模型或小规模观察性研究；FMT在CRC中的有效性尚未在随机对照试验中证实；不同肿瘤类型（如黑色素瘤 vs CRC）的微生物效应可能存在差异，不可直接外推。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组调节免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的具体实例和证据等级。明确指出Fn和Pa与抗PD-1治疗抵抗相关，而某些益生菌（如Bifidobacterium）在动物模型中增强ICI疗效。FMT在黑色素瘤中恢复ICI响应的临床证据被引用，但在CRC中仅为探索性试验。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于支持‘微生物组成分影响ICI疗效’这一观点，列举具体正负向影响的菌种，并说明当前临床转化的阶段（实验性）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制描述多为细胞或动物模型层面的因果推断；人类体内确切的因果链条仍需更多验证；不同菌株亚型（如Fn的不同clades）可能有不同效应。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物影响免疫微环境的分子机制。包括：1) Fn通过Fap2结合TIGIT抑制T/NK细胞毒性；2) Pa通过TLR2/4激活MDSC抑制CD8+/CD4+ T细胞；3) ETBF诱导Th17/IL-17炎症反应；4) 有益菌代谢物（SCFAs）调节树突状细胞/T细胞反应。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于解释微生物组调节ICI疗效的具体生物学通路，特别是免疫抑制性微环境的形成机制（TIGIT, MDSC, Th17等）。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何影响实体瘤（特别是结直肠癌）免疫治疗响应提供了关键的背景机制和现状评估。它详细列出了可能增强或削弱免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的微生物特征（如Fn富集导致耐药，特定益生菌增强疗效），并指出了FMT联合ICI治疗的潜在前景及当前证据局限。这对于回答微生物组调节ICI疗效的机制和现状至关重要。\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"作者将FMT在CRC中的应用严格限定为‘实验性/临床试验阶段’，不得将其解读为已确立的标准治疗。\",\n          \"文中提到的抗生素与CRC风险增加的相关性是流行病学观察结果，不能直接推导为因果关系用于个体临床决策，且明确反对将抗生素作为CRC治疗策略。\",\n          \"不同研究中对微生物标志物的定义和检测方法差异巨大，综述中引用的AUC值仅在各自研究背景下有效，跨研究比较需谨慎。\",\n          \"机制描述多基于小鼠模型或细胞实验，人类体内的确切效力和剂量效应尚不明确。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) and immune evasion\",\n          \"Peptostreptococcus anaerobius (Pa) and anti-PD-1 resistance\",\n          \"Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) in oncology\",\n          \"Microbiome modulation of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n          \"Strain-level SNVs in CRC detection\",\n          \"Short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) and immune homeostasis\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-f45b87be8e30256e\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\phase_iii_rct_evidence\\\\attempt-c7j_i2fn\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_a86301e06d\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n      \"year\": \"2025\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"P0605\"\n      ],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"采用前瞻性队列设计。收集接受ICI治疗的癌症患者粪便样本。使用16S rRNA测序和MGS进行微生物组分析。定义七个基于文献的预设细菌组（包括致病菌组和Ruminococcaceae等）。使用多种统计工具（ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2）进行差异丰度分析，以寻找跨工具一致的结果。通过逻辑回归和线性混合效应模型评估细菌组与严重irAE的关联，并校正ICI类型。比较有/无严重irAE患者在基线、治疗早期、irAE发作时及免疫抑制后的微生物组特征。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了大样本（195例）前瞻性数据，证实了Ruminococcaceae科的动态减少与严重irAE的相关性，特别是在irAE发作时的显著降低。\",\n            \"limits\": \"基线致病菌组的高RA关联在多重检验校正后不显著；部分低丰度菌群的差异结果需谨慎解读；无法区分菌株特异性效应；样本量对于解析复杂的多重交互作用仍显不足。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"基线（ICI治疗前）\",\n            \"finding\": \"发生严重irAE的患者中，预设的致病菌组（pathobionts）平均RA显著高于未发生者（8.2% vs 4.8%; OR 1.40; 95%CI 1.07-1.87），但该关联在多重检验校正后失去统计学显著性（校正p=0.059）。Ruminococcaceae科在两组间基线RA无显著差异。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"治疗早期（从基线到第2周期）\",\n            \"finding\": \"发生严重irAE的患者中，Ruminococcaceae科的RA下降幅度显著大于未发生者（交互作用粗p=0.018，校正p=0.123）。然而，发生组内的下降本身未达到统计学显著性（粗p=0.078）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"严重irAE发作时\",\n            \"finding\": \"与所有其他时间点相比，发生严重irAE的患者中Ruminococcaceae科、Ruminococcus属以及R. bromii和R. callidus物种的RA显著降低。Haemophilus属及其种H. parainfluenzae在irAE发作时的RA显著升高。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组可能影响ICI疗效，但其与严重irAEs的关联尚不明确，且既往研究结果存在冲突。本研究试图确定基线微生物特征或治疗期间的动态变化是否能预测严重irAEs，并探索潜在的病理生理机制。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"荷兰乌得勒支大学医学中心进行的UNI-CIT前瞻性生物库研究中的癌症患者。研究对象为接受一线抗PD-1单药或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4治疗的实体瘤患者（主要为黑色素瘤和非小细胞肺癌）。样本包括治疗前基线、治疗早期（第2-3周期）、严重irAE发作时及免疫抑制治疗后的粪便样本。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本研究旨在评估肠道微生物组在免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗开始时的组成及其在治疗过程中的变化，是否与随后发生的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs，≥3级）相关。通过对195名患者的497个粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序和宏基因组鸟枪法测序（MGS），分析α/β多样性、特定分类群相对丰度（RA）及预设细菌组的差异。研究发现，虽然基线时致病菌组（pathobionts）的RA较高与严重irAE风险增加有关（但在多重检验校正后不再显著），但Ruminococcaceae科在发生严重irAE的患者中表现出更显著的下降趋势，且在irAE发作时其RA显著低于其他时间点。这表明以Ruminococcaceae减少为特征的微生物组失调可能预示严重irAE的发生。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文提供了关于肠道微生物组动态变化（特别是Ruminococcaceae科的减少）与ICI诱导的严重毒性（irAEs）之间关联的直接实证证据。它强调了微生物组在irAE发病机制中的潜在角色，并指出了单一物种（如F. prausnitzii）研究的局限性，支持从群落水平（如科/属）或功能失衡角度理解irAEs。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅观察性关联，非因果证明；主要关注毒性而非直接疗效指标（如ORR/PFS）；结果受多重检验校正影响。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组组成变化与ICI疗效/毒性关联的观察性证据。具体发现Ruminococcaceae科的减少与严重irAEs相关，提示微生物组状态可能调节宿主对ICI的反应谱（不仅限于抗肿瘤疗效，还包括毒性）。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中讨论微生物组如何影响ICI的整体临床结局（疗效与毒性并存），作为微生物组介导ICI反应性的证据之一。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制推断为主，缺乏直接的分子机制验证（如代谢物测量或动物实验验证）；F. prausnitzii的具体作用在该研究中未得到明确支持（基线无差异）。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"探讨了可能的机制线索：致病菌组富集和有益菌（Ruminococcaceae）减少导致的菌群失调（dysbiosis）可能促进炎症反应，从而引发irAEs。特别讨论了F. prausnitzii（产丁酸菌）在不同研究中的矛盾结果，暗示菌株特异性的重要性。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中解释微生物组介导irAEs的潜在机制假说，特别是短链脂肪酸（如丁酸）产生菌的作用及菌株特异性差异。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"帮助综述构建“微生物组失衡导致irAEs”的理论框架，同时提醒读者注意低丰度菌群结果的可靠性问题。\",\n            \"material\": \"基线致病菌组高RA与irAE风险的初步关联（虽校正后不显著，但趋势一致），以及H. parainfluenzae在irAE发作时的升高。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为背景材料，说明微生物组中不同菌群（促炎vs抗炎）平衡的重要性，以及单一标志物预测的复杂性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"用于综述的方法学讨论部分，强调当前微生物组研究在标准化、菌株分辨率方面的挑战。\",\n            \"material\": \"对F. prausnitzii在既往研究中矛盾结果的详细讨论。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"提供领域内争议实例，说明为什么需要更精细的菌株水平分析或标准化方法。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"基线致病菌组与irAE的关联在多重检验校正后不显著，不能视为确证的保护/风险因素，仅为趋势。\",\n          \"Ruminococcaceae的减少是观察到的关联，不等于因果关系；可能是irAE的前驱标志或伴随现象。\",\n          \"低丰度菌群（如Marvinbryantia, Haemophilus）的差异结果可能存在技术噪音，需谨慎引用。\",\n          \"研究未直接测量ICI疗效（如肿瘤缩小），因此不能直接推断微生物组对疗效的影响，仅能推断对毒性的影响。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Ruminococcaceae科动态变化\",\n          \"致病菌组（Pathobionts）基线丰度\",\n          \"严重irAEs（≥3级）预测因子\",\n          \"16S rRNA与MGS联合分析\",\n          \"多工具差异丰度验证（ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2）\",\n          \"F. prausnitzii争议性结果对比\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study employed a robust methodological framework useful for review methodology discussions, including longitudinal sampling (baseline, during treatment, at irAE onset, post-immunosuppression), both 16S rRNA and metagenomic shotgun sequencing, and multiple differential abundance tools (ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2) to ensure consistency. The authors discuss limitations regarding sample size for specific taxa and the need for correction for multiple testing, which resulted in some baseline associations (e.g., pathobionts) losing significance after correction.\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_3\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-hpbnytrx\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_4736138316\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"Use this study in the review to illustrate the current state of evidence: even recent prospective cohorts (2025) with nearly 200 patients must aggregate irAE types due to low incidence of specific non-colitis toxicities. Cite the specific sample counts for myocarditis and meningitis from Table 1 and Section 3.6 to substantiate the claim that large-scale specific data is still lacking. Leverage the methodological details (longitudinal design, multi-tool analysis) as a benchmark for future study recommendations.\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for large-scale microbiome association studies specifically targeting non-colitis irAEs (e.g., myocarditis, neurotoxicity) to verify evidence insufficiency. This study does not fulfill that requirement because it aggregates all severe irAEs into one group; the specific counts for non-colitis irAEs like myocarditis (n=2) and meningitis (n=2) are too small for independent large-scale association analysis. Thus, the existence of a dedicated large-scale study for non-colitis irAE microbiome signatures remains unconfirmed by this material.\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"This prospective cohort study (Verheijden et al., 2025) analyzed 497 stool samples from 195 cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) to assess gut microbiome associations with severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The study included various irAE types listed in Table 1, such as myocarditis (n=2 total), meningitis (n=2 total), pneumonitis (n=4 total), and colitis (n=6 total), but aggregated them into a single 'severe irAE' endpoint for analysis due to low incidence of individual types. Key findings indicated that a higher baseline relative abundance of a prespecified pathobiont group and a stronger decrease in Ruminococcaceae during treatment were associated with developing severe irAEs. At irAE onset, Ruminococcaceae and specific species (R. bromii, R. callidus) were significantly lower, while Haemophilus parainfluenzae was higher compared to other time points. The authors explicitly note in Section 3.6 that only 17 patients provided samples at severe irAE onset, with diverse irAE types (8 colitis, 3 pancreatitis/diabetes, 2 meningitis, 4 others), limiting subtype-specific analysis.\"\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch6.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\\\\e9a69606b703c06cd1c1d609fc8e8730\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\\\\e9a69606b703c06cd1c1d609fc8e8730\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"planning_revision_mode\": true,\n  \"citation_number_map_origin\": \"generated_local_aliases\",\n  \"citation_number_map\": {\n    \"0011\": \"P0011\",\n    \"0017\": \"P0017\",\n    \"0040\": \"P0040\",\n    \"0049\": \"P0049\",\n    \"0067\": \"P0067\",\n    \"0088\": \"P0088\",\n    \"0146\": \"P0146\",\n    \"0197\": \"P0197\",\n    \"0212\": \"P0212\",\n    \"0261\": \"P0261\",\n    \"0284\": \"P0284\",\n    \"0297\": \"P0297\",\n    \"0310\": \"P0310\",\n    \"0314\": \"P0314\",\n    \"0319\": \"P0319\",\n    \"0357\": \"P0357\",\n    \"0409\": \"P0409\",\n    \"0447\": \"P0447\",\n    \"0460\": \"P0460\",\n    \"0462\": \"P0462\",\n    \"0486\": \"P0486\",\n    \"0578\": \"P0578\",\n    \"0583\": \"P0583\",\n    \"0590\": \"P0590\",\n    \"0595\": \"P0595\",\n    \"0596\": \"P0596\",\n    \"0597\": \"P0597\",\n    \"0598\": \"P0598\",\n    \"0600\": \"P0600\",\n    \"0601\": \"P0601\",\n    \"0602\": \"P0602\",\n    \"0604\": \"P0604\",\n    \"0605\": \"P0605\",\n    \"0609\": \"P0609\",\n    \"11\": \"P0011\",\n    \"146\": \"P0146\",\n    \"17\": \"P0017\",\n    \"197\": \"P0197\",\n    \"212\": \"P0212\",\n    \"261\": \"P0261\",\n    \"284\": \"P0284\",\n    \"297\": \"P0297\",\n    \"310\": \"P0310\",\n    \"314\": \"P0314\",\n    \"319\": \"P0319\",\n    \"357\": \"P0357\",\n    \"40\": \"P0040\",\n    \"409\": \"P0409\",\n    \"447\": \"P0447\",\n    \"460\": \"P0460\",\n    \"462\": \"P0462\",\n    \"486\": \"P0486\",\n    \"49\": \"P0049\",\n    \"578\": \"P0578\",\n    \"583\": \"P0583\",\n    \"590\": \"P0590\",\n    \"595\": \"P0595\",\n    \"596\": \"P0596\",\n    \"597\": \"P0597\",\n    \"598\": \"P0598\",\n    \"600\": \"P0600\",\n    \"601\": \"P0601\",\n    \"602\": \"P0602\",\n    \"604\": \"P0604\",\n    \"605\": \"P0605\",\n    \"609\": \"P0609\",\n    \"67\": \"P0067\",\n    \"88\": \"P0088\"\n  }\n}"
